		{
			dependencies: ["3A98FA709F0DEA42"]
			description: [
				"As you can see, Create, as a technology-based mod, has its own form of energy. Unlike other mods that rely on electricity or heat, Mechanical Power uses a concept known as &6Stress&r. &2It cannot be stored and must be consumed in real time as it is generated&r."
				""
				"Similar to the concepts of voltage and current, &2Torque&r and &2Rotational Speed&r are used to describe stress. Torque can be understood as rotational force, while speed represents how fast the rotation occurs. Different machines require different values of these parameters, so when a machine does not function properly, it is often necessary to check whether the stress supply itself is insufficient."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"To generate stress, the simplest method is using a &6Hand Crank&r to manually produce it. Of course, this is only a temporary solution."
				""
				"Another commonly used method is powering a &6Water Wheel&r, which is compact and can be modularly placed anywhere within an automation setup."
				""
				"If these options are not enough for your large-scale machinery, then using &6Steam Engine&r may be the only viable solution (or alternative power sources from Create's addons)."
			]
			hide_dependent_lines: true
			id: "24EEB667413FCADC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1E095763EC83A366"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
					tag: { }
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Most common souce for rotational force"
			tasks: [{
				id: "24C67EC8810E98BB"
				item: "create:windmill_bearing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Water Wheel, Windmill and Rotational Force (Stress)"
			x: 0.75d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4EB8FE041AB6DA8E"]
			description: [
				"The main ores used in Create are copper, iron, and the mod’s own ore, &6Zinc Ore&r. These play a important role throughout all stages of Create progression."
				""
				"However, you do not need to stockpile large amounts of these ores, as Create does not consume resources at a particularly high rate (unless you are building extremely large-scale structures). In fact, as mentioned earlier, &2Andesite&r is actually one of the scarcest early-game resources in this mod (iron can also be tight at the beginning)."
				""
				"With these materials, you can craft one of the most commonly used early-game alloys—&6Andesite Alloy&r."
			]
			hide_dependent_lines: true
			icon: "create:zinc_ingot"
			id: "3A98FA709F0DEA42"
			rewards: [{
				count: 3
				id: "6D9415D934A5ECBE"
